# SPA fallback. Read by Netlify and by Cloudflare Pages from the root of the published
# directory — Vite copies this file verbatim from public/ into .output/public/.
#
# Client-side routing owns every path, so a path the host has no file for must come back as the
# prerendered shell with a 200, not a 404. A non-forced 200 rule only fires when nothing on disk
# matches, so /assets/*, /icons/* and the manifest still serve themselves.
#
# `/` is covered by index.html on its own; this line exists for deep links such as
# /prototypes/motion and for anything the router adds later.
#
# The shell is emitted as index.html by `spa.prerender.outputPath` in vite.config.ts. If a build
# ever puts it back at /_shell.html, change the target below and nothing else.

/*    /index.html    200
